From 149f9481ccfc4e66159a8af487499768c1431c56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Ron D." <8740514+rgnv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:03:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/29] wip cleanup: strip W3DBG debug instrumentation

Remove the one-shot diagnostic prints left from the fog-of-war, world-pass
and spawn debugging sessions (fow-update/census counters, fow-send row
prints, cl_fow/cl_view/cl-fow compose probes, fogtex/revealer probes,
_W3M_DrawWorld/world-pass layer probes, SP_CallSpawn). No behavior change:
the reveal/send/loop logic is untouched, only counting and printing.
Keeper diagnostics (missing FDF bindings, failed loads, renderer warnings)
are unchanged; the dormant W3_FOWOFF headless override stays.
---
 client/cl_parse.c                         |  3 --
 client/cl_view.c                          |  2 --
 games/warcraft-3/game/g_fow.c             | 42 +++--------------------
 games/warcraft-3/game/g_spawn.c           | 10 ------
 games/warcraft-3/renderer/w3m/r_war3map.c |  2 --
 renderer/r_fogofwar.c                     |  6 ++--
 6 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

